IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`
IMPORT `fwa-day-one`
IMPORT `fwa-seat-employer`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (with the Fair Work Regulations 2009), day one -- the employer's seat layer, worked cases.
--
-- SEAT: the employer. Importing fwa-employee.l4, fwa-day-one.l4 and fwa-seat-employer.l4 together is itself the
-- first test: the three define no name twice.
--
-- Expected values were written by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the encoding's output. MIRROR cases
-- ask the same facts from both seats and assert each gives the same hand-worked answer.
--
-- d044 (2031-06-01): Daniel's Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd takes on its first three employees; Jarrah is a small
-- business employer (s 23(1): fewer than 15; 3 employees, 4 counting Daniel if he is employed by the company -- either
-- way under 15). The life says "contracts, super at 12%" and nothing about casual or fixed-term employment: those
-- facts are HYPOTHETICAL and marked.
-- c040 (2024-02-05): Ironbark Logistics Pty Ltd taking Chloe on, full-time and ongoing, with a probation clause.

§ `ss 44, 60, 61 -- the NES as a floor`

-- MIRROR. c040 / d044: a probation clause giving less than the NES cannot displace them (s 61(1)).
#ASSERT (`As the employer, can the contract give less than the NES` TRUE `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter` EQUALS `the NES apply in full: the term cannot displace them (s 61(1)), and acting on it would contravene s 44`) AND (`Can my contract give me less than the NES` TRUE `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter` EQUALS `the NES apply in full: the term cannot displace them (s 61(1)), and acting on it would contravene s 44`)
#ASSERT `As the employer, can the contract give less than the NES` TRUE `it gives the same as the NES, or more` EQUALS `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`
#ASSERT `As the employer, can the contract give less than the NES` FALSE `it gives the same as the NES, or more` EQUALS `not covered: the NES apply only to a national system employee (s 60)`

-- MIRROR. s 44.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, have I contravened the NES` TRUE TRUE) AND (`Has my employer contravened the NES` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, have I contravened the NES` TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 125, 125B, 333K -- the statements`

-- MIRROR. d044: a full-time permanent first employee: the Fair Work Information Statement only (s 125(1)).
#ASSERT (`As the employer, which statements must I give on day one` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`)) AND (`Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`))
-- MIRROR. d044, "what must I give a new casual on day one?" (HYPOTHETICAL casual): both statements (ss 125(1),
-- 125B(1)(a)).
#ASSERT (`As the employer, which statements must I give on day one` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`, `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`)) AND (`Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`, `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`))
-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL casual on a fixed term): all three.
#ASSERT `As the employer, which statements must I give on day one` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`, `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`, `the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (s 333K)`)
-- A contractor, not a national system employee: not covered.
#ASSERT `As the employer, which statements must I give on day one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: these duties are owed only to a national system employee`

-- MIRROR. s 125.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I give the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE) AND (`Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, must I give the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE TRUE

-- MIRROR. d044 (HYPOTHETICAL casual; Jarrah with 3 employees, small): at 6 months no statement (s 125B(2)).
#ASSERT (NOT `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `6 months after starting` 3 FALSE) AND (NOT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `6 months after starting` 3 FALSE)
-- MIRROR. At 12 months, yes (s 125B(1)(c)(i), which s 125B(2) does not reach).
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `12 months after starting` 3 FALSE) AND (`Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `12 months after starting` 3 FALSE)
-- At the start, yes (s 125B(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `starting as a casual` 3 FALSE
-- After each further 12 months, no while small; yes at 15 (s 23(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `the end of each further 12 months` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `the end of each further 12 months` 15 FALSE
-- Not a casual: never.
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` FALSE TRUE `starting as a casual` 3 FALSE

§ `s 535, regs 3.31-3.42 -- records`

-- MIRROR. d044: a full-time salaried first employee, entitled to leave, super at 12%: reg 3.32 basics, reg 3.33(1)
-- pay, reg 3.36(1) leave, reg 3.37 super.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, what records must I keep` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`, `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`, `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`, `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`) AND (`What records must my employer keep about me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`, `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`, `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`, `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`)
-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL casual paid by the hour with a casual loading): six kinds -- add hours (reg 3.33(2)) and the
-- loading (reg 3.33(3)).
#ASSERT `As the employer, what records must I keep` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`, `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`, `the hours worked (reg 3.33(2))`, `details of each incentive payment, bonus, loading, penalty rate or allowance (reg 3.33(3))`, `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`, `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`
-- With no condition met, the two kinds every employee has (regs 3.32, 3.33(1)).
#ASSERT count (`As the employer, what records must I keep` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 2

-- MIRROR. d044, "for how long?": 7 years (s 535(1)).
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how many years must I keep records` EQUALS 7) AND (`How many years must my employer keep my records` EQUALS 7)
-- A record made 7 years ago may go; one made 6.5 years ago may not (READING: counted from when it was made).
#ASSERT `As the employer, may I stop keeping this record` 7
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, may I stop keeping this record` 6.5

-- Reg 3.31(1): legible, English, readily accessible to an inspector.
#ASSERT `As the employer, is my record in the required form` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, is my record in the required form` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, is my record in the required form` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- MIRROR. Reg 3.42: Jarrah keeps its records off-site (HYPOTHETICAL, in the cloud): as soon as practicable.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how quickly must I produce a record` FALSE EQUALS `as soon as practicable, at the workplace or by post (reg 3.42(4))`) AND (`How quickly must I be shown my records` FALSE EQUALS `as soon as practicable, at the workplace or by post (reg 3.42(4))`)
#ASSERT `As the employer, how quickly must I produce a record` TRUE EQUALS `within 3 business days at the workplace, or posted within 14 days (reg 3.42(3))`

§ `s 536 -- pay slips`

-- s 536(1): within one working day of paying.
#ASSERT `As the employer, was my pay slip in time` 1
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, was my pay slip in time` 2

§ `s 557C -- no records`

-- MIRROR. No leave record kept, an NES claim, no excuse accepted: the employer must disprove it.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I disprove the allegation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) AND (`Must my employer disprove what I allege` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, must I disprove the allegation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A claim under a provision s 557C(3) does not list (say an unfair dismissal remedy): no reversal.
#ASSERT NOT `As the employer, must I disprove the allegation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
